e Deceived what to stop them then thinking that there \u2018just\u2019 claimed by really powerful spirits a werewolf is not going to know about the Subtle differences between them I can\u2019t imagine that the will be secretly talking notes also, I don\u2019t think werewolves care all that much about semantics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 05-21-2019, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:35:51-08:00","id":1189894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1189887-storm-lords-vs-deceived?p=1189892#post1189892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do know that werewolves don\u2019t have book of spirt and book of the Deceived what to stop them then thinking that there \u2018just\u2019 claimed by really powerful spirts,a werewolf is not going to know about the sudden differences betwreen them I can\u2019t imagine that the will be secretly talking notes , and I don\u2019t think werewolves care all that much about semantics</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't have the books, but they do have powers that explicitly detect things using Fetter, Claim, and so forth, and Deceived aren't called out as using them.<br /> <br /> But they would lump them in with them. Sin-Eaters, for instance, are not made using Claim, they're made using Bargain, but would likely be considered close enough to warrant destruction (unless they were convinced otherwise). It's also entirely possible they might get along with the Deceived and let them into their pack or even join their cult. It brings up Werewolf and Mummy interactions in the Pack, though it doesn't get into the Deceived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:41:23-08:00","id":1189895,"title":"","content":"but would likely be considered close enough to warrant destruction (unless they were convinced otherwise). But why not decided they seem close enough to Warnet desctruction especcly if there fucking about on the packs terrority<br /> . But I maybe can see some wolves joining a cult of the keeper . Maybe they had there. First change in the cult,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:44:59-08:00","id":1189896,"title":"","content":"Besides I think some powerful spirts can hide themselves from powers like that . I think the pack would just assume that they just have a special power that lets them to go undetected","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:47:25-08:00","id":1189899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1189887-storm-lords-vs-deceived?p=1189895#post1189895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but would likely be considered close enough to warrant destruction (unless they were convinced otherwise). But why not decided they seem close enough to Warnet desctruction especcly if there fucking about on the packs terrority</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, it wouldn't even matter if they were Claimed if they were really messing things up or causing trouble, they'd just be a target for the sacred hunt.<br /> <br /> There's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1169158-twelve-storm-lords-bowing?p=1169611#post1169611\">an interesting pack</a> with a variety of plot hooks revolving around a (non-the Curse) mummy and one option that might lean more towards it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Guayota has become a disembodied spirit, roving far and wide on strange and bizarre affairs. Now, however, it has returned its attention to the real world, and wishes to return to existence. It is manipulating the Tibicenas into performing something akin to the Rite of Return used by the Shaniatu of Irem, having pried that lore loose from the world on its travels. It plans to establish itself as a ghost-king, with the Tibicenas as cursed wolf-mummies grovelling before its throne. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:52:05-08:00","id":1189901,"title":"","content":"I wonder what will happen I\u2019m imfnaing a scenario where a mummy fighting a Amkhata or something and a cultist there suddenly has there first change and tear it to shreds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:56:26-08:00","id":1189904,"title":"","content":"Personally, i think that without more profound knowledge, most of the other splats (vamps, etc) would feel rather like Claimed for the Storm Lords. Not necessarily a majority of the tribe but on a person by person basis, i'd say more than a few. If that make any sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T09:57:49-08:00","id":1189907,"title":"","content":"I think there a storm lord stertype where a leach claimed is mistaken for a vampire .can you think what storm lords would think of the strix the will be absolutely furious what if strip posses some vamps and make them fight werewolves so the werewolves and campers fight that a pretty stryixy thing right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 02-27-2018, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T10:59:41-08:00","id":1189932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1189887-storm-lords-vs-deceived?p=1189904#post1189904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, i think that without more profound knowledge, most of the other splats (vamps, etc) would feel rather like Claimed for the Storm Lords. Not necessarily a majority of the tribe but on a person by person basis, i'd say more than a few. If that make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and apparently a lot of the stuff can fall to regional locales, there's some folklore that says vampires are dead werewolves, for instance, and it would be easy to think of any game as a Claimed or special kind of Host.<br /> <br /> But mechanically you wouldn't be able to use an ability that targets only spirits or only Claimed on a vampire, which would clue them in but not be the end-all of things, as they could just be a special variant that, for whatever reason, is immune to those types of abilities.<br /> <br /> It helps that werewolves aren't locked into their sacred prey, and they're capable of hunting whatever needs to be hunted, rather than only hunting one kind of monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T11:35:03-08:00","id":1189953,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s just what I said","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T11:36:11-08:00","id":1189955,"title":"","content":"According to some theories about the strix vampires could be a type of claimed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T14:21:25-08:00","id":1190008,"title":"","content":"Whould strix posessed vampire be considered claimed ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T21:32:59-08:00","id":1190133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1189887-storm-lords-vs-deceived?p=1190008#post1190008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whould strix posessed vampire be considered claimed ?</div> </div> </div> </div>They use a different ability, and they're not spirits, so mechanically no. But they'd probably be lumped in with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T03:23:14-08:00","id":1190189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1189887-storm-lords-vs-deceived?p=1190133#post1190133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They use a different ability, and they're not spirits, so mechanically no. But they'd probably be lumped in with them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves, like humans, prefer things in their boxes. Even (especially?) when it doesn't fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T04:06:36-08:00","id":1190194,"title":"","content":"Werewolves don\u2019t debate semantics if a ethereal being posses a dude and causes mayhym they\u2019ll think will look it\u2019s a owl/sadist Claimed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T05:57:49-08:00","id":1190226,"title":"","content":"I kind of want to list a joke &quot;Werewolf Prey Logic&quot; flow chart. Like ((IsHuman) ? Iron Masters : [continue question chain]).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T07:03:26-08:00","id":1190254,"title":"","content":"Alright so how would a pack of werewolves fight a mummy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:27:49-08:00","id":1190280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1189887-storm-lords-vs-deceived?p=1190254#post1190254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright so how would a pack of werewolves fight a mummy</div> </div> </div> </div>With tooth and claw.<br /> <br /> More seriously - it depends on A) How much they know about Mummies B) The werewolves' Tribe C) How strong their Pack is D) How strong the Mummy is E) How much do they know of C &amp; D.<br /> <br /> Mummies dislike Fire, have few options against non-Ghost things in Twilight, and grow weaker over time. They have crazy healing powers, awesome powers in Utterances (and a few Affinities), and maybe Relics. And can't be permanently put down.<br /> <br /> If the Pack has friendly Fire Spirits, and/or access to the Tongue of Fire Facet of the Gift of Elements, they can bring the hurt. If not, they'll need Relic weaponry. Note that Mummies can keep fighting even when they should be destroyed as long as they have Pillar points to spend on Sealing the Flesh.<br /> <br /> Cultists vs Pack Members washes out since Mummy Cultists are typically vulnerable to Lunacy, and non-Uratha Pack members are vulnerable to Sybaris.<br /> <br /> Their best bet it to manipulate Spirits and hostile/disposable groups to harass and burn the Mummy out. If they can end the current Descent, next arising, the Mummy should only be angry at their dupes, and not the Pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 02-28-2018, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:45:12-08:00","id":1190289,"title":"","content":"Would they win ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:52:40-08:00","id":1190292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1189887-storm-lords-vs-deceived?p=1190289#post1190289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would they win ?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Yes. Maybe. It Depends.<br /> <br /> You really need to clarify the conditions and goals before that 